# Input
```vue
<script setup>
/* should generate diagnostics */
const emit = defineEmits([`click`, "change"]);
emit(`click`);
emit("keydown");
(emit)?.("CHANGE");
</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-script-setup.vue:3:27 lint/nursery/noVueShadowNativeEvents ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This component event shadows the native click event.
  
    1 │ <script setup>
    2 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 3 │ const emit = defineEmits([`click`, "change"]);
      │                           ^^^^^^^
    4 │ emit(`click`);
    5 │ emit("keydown");
  
  i Component events don't bubble, carry an arbitrary payload, and don't support event modifiers that rely on a native event, so listeners written for the native click event can misbehave.
  
  i Rename the event after what happened in the component.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

